@startuml
title ASII-13 - Semana 5: arquitectura cliente-servidor actual

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Personal clinico" as Clinico

rectangle "Cliente web existente" {
  [Vue 3] as Vue
  [Vue Router / Pinia] as ClientState
  [Axios] as Axios
}

rectangle "Monolito modular Laravel" {
  [TenantMiddleware] as Tenant
  [JwtAuth] as Jwt
  [VitalSignController] as Controller
  [StoreVitalSignRequest] as Request
  [VitalSignRegistrationService] as Service
  [VitalSignRangeEvaluator] as Evaluator
  interface "VitalSignRangeProvider\n(sin implementacion/binding)" as RangeProvider
  [EloquentVitalSignRepository] as Repository
}

rectangle "Modelos HIS relacionados" {
  [VitalSign] as VitalSign
  [MedicalRecord] as MedicalRecord
  [Admission] as Admission
  [User] as User
  [Tenant] as TenantModel
}

database "HOSPITAL\n(vital_signs y datos clinicos)" as Hospital

Clinico --> Vue
Vue --> ClientState
Vue --> Axios
Axios --> Tenant : HTTP JSON\nBearer JWT + X-Tenant-ID
Tenant --> TenantModel : resuelve tenant
Tenant --> Jwt
Jwt --> User : autentica JWT y valida tenant
Jwt --> Controller
Controller --> Request : valida body
Controller --> Service : tenant y usuario confiables
Service --> Repository
Service --> RangeProvider : consulta rango aprobado
Service --> Evaluator : evalua mediciones
Repository --> VitalSign
VitalSign --> MedicalRecord
VitalSign --> Admission
Repository --> Hospital

note right of Controller
Ruta registrada:
POST /api/v1/vital-signs

No existe UI especifica ASII-13
ni permisos ASII-13 aplicados.
end note

note bottom of Hospital
Propiedad logica: HOSPITAL.
tenant_id delimita los datos clinicos.
CENTRAL no recibe signos vitales clinicos.
end note

@enduml
